From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winusb.sys, wineusb.sys: The WinUSB driver, and devices that declare it (6520)

A function driver, winusb.sys, over wineusb's device objects: it
selects the interface's first setting, registers the device interfaces
the device names, and serves winusb.dll's IOCTLs with URBs (control,
bulk and interrupt transfers that can be cancelled, pipe resets and
aborts, alternate settings). wineusb reads each device's Microsoft OS
descriptors (1.0 and 2.0): a device or interface declaring the
compatible ID "WINUSB" gets USB\MS_COMP_WINUSB, which winusb.inf
matches, and the DeviceInterfaceGUID it names; an administrator may
list more devices under HKLM\Software\Stained Glass\WinUSB\Devices.
wineusb also gains the remaining control URBs (any control transfer,
GET_STATUS, SET/CLEAR_FEATURE, vendor and class requests to endpoints
and others), SELECT_INTERFACE, and cancellation of pending transfers.
Device permissions are unchanged: only devices the user can already
open are seen.
